    "background_story": "Autumn was a brilliant and fearless surgeon in the 19th century. She pioneered the use of thermocautery, a revolutionary technique that utilized heat to treat various medical conditions. Autumn's fascination with thermocautery began when she witnessed its effectiveness in treating her own brother's wounds during the war. She dedicated her life to mastering the technique, experimenting with different temperatures and applications. Autumn's groundbreaking work led to the development of new treatments for ailments such as ulcers and tumors. Her expertise earned her recognition among the medical community, and she became a sought-after lecturer and instructor. Autumn's innovative approach to thermocautery not only saved countless lives but also paved the way for future generations of surgeons.",
